CHANGE 6 (README.txt, CHANGE 6):
  - MAX_WAYPOINTS 1024 -> 4096, for one waypoint set over h9_tsrp_hive's three
    cities. A waypoint file with more than that is refused instead of read past
    the end of the waypoint array.
  - The visibility table is saved as visibility/<mod>/<map>.rcv2, packed
    num x num, so the file no longer depends on MAX_WAYPOINTS. An old .rcv is
    never read; each map works its table out once more on its first load. (The
    .rcv save kept only the first num*num bits of the MAX_WAYPOINTS-wide table,
    so every row past num*num/MAX_WAYPOINTS was lost, and its load cleared 4 bytes
    of the table instead of all of it.)
  - Waypoints farther apart than BOT_VIEW_DISTANCE (2048) are not traced for the
    table -- never visible to each other -- which keeps a big map's first load short.
  - TS breakable doors: a door with "maxdamage" (TS gives it DAMAGE_YES) that the
    line to a bot's next waypoint meets within 96 units is taken as a target, at
    a func_breakable's priority (5), until TS shatters it: the bot shoots it down
    and walks on. EntityIsAlive counts such a door as standing until TS sets it
    DEAD_DEAD and DAMAGE_NO.

